y}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpccelon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"mpccelon","id":39243838,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MjQzODM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39243838?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpccelon","html_url":"https://github.com/mpccelon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpccelon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpccelon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpccelon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpccelon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpccelon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpccelon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpccelon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpccelon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpccelon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"95cf22e59f7b791fe04024d0e0e363d0bc3d662d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mpccelon/hardware-accelerated-hog-svm/commits/95cf22e59f7b791fe04024d0e0e363d0bc3d662d","html_url":"https://github.com/mpccelon/hardware-accelerated-hog-svm/commit/95cf22e59f7b791fe04024d0e0e363d0bc3d662d"}],"stats":{"total":24,"additions":21,"deletions":3},"files":[{"sha":"1a7f6a9cfb57e73e572990bc9e34b0ce73c8280e","filename":"README.md","status":"modified","additions":14,"deletions":2,"changes":16,"blob_url":"https://github.com/mpccelon/hardware-accelerated-hog-svm/blob/56bb5d5c01f566797486dc2f37d25fa61e81b3d6/README.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/mpccelon/hardware-accelerated-hog-svm/raw/56bb5d5c01f566797486dc2f37d25fa61e81b3d6/README.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mpccelon/hardware-accelerated-hog-svm/contents/README.md?ref=56bb5d5c01f566797486dc2f37d25fa61e81b3d6","patch":"@@ -5,6 +5,8 @@ Created for our undergraduate thesis project dealing with dynamic traffic manage\n # Results\n The FPGA hardware acceleration achieves a **13x** speedup compared to the software Raspberry Pi implementation. While this does result in decreased robustness (decrease in F1/MCC scores), the throughput increase in the resulting [dynamic traffic managment simulation](https://gitlab.com/pgilaga/ITMS-UCL04) is still maintained.\n \n+# Details\n+\n Implemented using the ff:\n * [Digilent Zybo with Zynq 7000 All-Programmable SoC](https://reference.digilentinc.com/reference/programmable-logic/zybo/start)\n * [Raspberry Pi 3](https://www.raspberrypi.org/products/raspberry-pi-3-model-b/)\n@@ -13,7 +15,7 @@ Implemented using the ff:\n Contains the datasets used for training and testing. Increasing sampled dataset as of May 17, 2018.\n \n ## hog_svm_fpga\n-The hardware implementation of the HOG-SVM algorithm, done in HLS C++. Vivado HLS WebPACK 2018.1 project.\n+The hardware implementation of the HOG-SVM algorithm, done in HLS C++. Vivado HLS WebPACK 2018.1 project. The integrated Xillybus IP core is also included, in a Vivado project folder. \n \n ## interface\n The software wrapper for the Zybo, along with interaction with the rest of the traffic management network\n@@ -25,4 +27,14 @@ Implementation, training, and testing of the HOG-SVM algorithm for deskops. Visu\n Benchmarking of the hardware implementation of the HOG-SVM algorithm. Includes benchmarking for RasPi embedded systems  \n \n ## results\n-Results collated so far, along with the draft of the overall thesis project.  \n\\ No newline at end of file\n+Results collated so far, along with the draft of the overall thesis project.  \n+\n+# Step by Step Guide\n+\n+1. Install [Vivado HLS](https://www.xilinx.com/products/design-tools/vivado/vivado-webpack.html). The WebPACK edition is fine, if you're using boards like the Zybo.\n+2. Install [Xillinux](http://xillybus.com/downloads/doc/xillybus_getting_started_zynq.pdf) for the Zynq Zybo, or the Zynq board of your choice. If not using a Zynq board, refer to the [Xillybus Documentation](http://xillybus.com/doc) for information on the specific board.\n+3. Compile [OpenCV 3.4.1](https://opencv.org/releases.html) for both the PC and the Zynq board. CUDA support is optional for the PC, but very helpful when trying out different features. If using Windows, also install [Visual Studio](https://www.visualstudio.com/) the benchmark tools are in a Visual Studio solution. Read the [Windows](https://docs.opencv.org/3.4/d3/d52/tutorial_windows_install.html) or [Linux](https://docs.opencv.org/trunk/d7/d9f/tutorial_linux_install.html) compile instructions.\n+4. Follow the [co-processing guide](http://xillybus.com/tutorials/vivado-hls-c-fpga-howto-1) for generating the bitstream. The [Vivado HLS project folder](hog_svm_fpga/README.md) and the [Xillybus Vivado project folder](hog_svm_fpga/Xillybus_bitstream) is already included in the project.\n+5. Load the custom bitstream to the Zynq board.\n+6. Compile the [interface program](interface/vehicle_detector.cpp). Use the Makefile provided. Note that it uses the C++ 2014 standard.\n+7. Run the interface program to connect with the rest of the program.\n\\ No newline at end of file"},{"sha":"18b189247a6548efd1d635c2d3ffcdd4990c7d4d","filename":"hog_svm_fpga/README.md","status":"modified","additions":7,"deletions":1,"changes":8,"blob_url":"https://github.com/mpccelon/hardware-accelerated-hog-svm/blob/56bb5d5c01f566797486dc2f37d25fa61e81b3d6/hog_svm_fpga%2FREADME.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/mpccelon/hardware-accelerated-hog-svm/raw/56bb5d5c01f566797486dc2f37d25fa61e81b3d6/hog_svm_fpga%2FREADME.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mpccelon/hardware-accelerated-hog-svm/contents/hog_svm_fpga%2FREADME.md?ref=56bb5d5c01f566797486dc2f37d25fa61e81b3d6","patch":"@@ -1,4 +1,10 @@\n # HOG-SVM implementation on the Digilent ZYBO board\n Implemented using the Xilinx Vivado HLS WebPACK 2018.1 IDE.  \n The [Xillybus IP core](xillybus.com) was used for faster deployment, transforming data communication into 32-bit FIFOs.  \n-Final product takes in a 64x64 detection window, and returns a confidence value. A positive value implies the window contains a vehicle.\n+Final product takes in a 64x64 detection window, and returns a confidence value. A positive value implies the window contains a vehicle.  \n+\n+# Step by step instructions for generating the bitstream \n+\n+1. Open this folder as a Vivado HLS project, and synthesize the Design Checkpoint (.dcp) file.\n+2. Open the Xillybus_bitstream folder in Vivado, and add the synthesized .dcp file as a source. It should load as all of the xillybus_wrapper modules.\n+3. Generate the bitstream."},{"sha":"1cdb8e67dcf836b7bd1b97099fe5428bc3c4c4b6","filename":"results/UCL_04_Final_Presentation.pdf","status":"added","additions":0,"deletions":0,"changes":0,"blob_url":"https://github.com/mpccelon/hardware-accelerated-hog-svm/blob/56bb5d5c01f566797486dc2f37d25fa61e81b3d6/results%2FUCL_04_Final_Presentation.pdf","raw_url":"https://github.com/mpccelon/hardware-accelerated-hog-svm/raw/56bb5d5c01f566797486dc2f37d25fa61e81b3d6/results%2FUCL_04_Final_Presentation.pdf","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mpccelon/hardware-accelerated-hog-svm/contents/results%2FUCL_04_Final_Presentation.pdf?ref=56bb5d5c01f566797486dc2f37d25fa61e81b3d6"}]}